  "readme": "# Rowdy original resources and shared-player registration\n\nRestore four missing original MOC/PNG files for rowdy01/rowdy02 and register two models, both52-entry member maps and54 package records. Existing descriptor/motion/detail, preview gzip/WebP and player indexes remain unchanged. Independent source-image identity review does not accept acting, phase, expressions or full gameplay; no new character field is installed here. The original binaries live under assets/models and match the sealed stage hashes rather than being duplicated in this audit. Existing gzip MOCs inflate byte-exact to those originals. Existing WebP is retained; no historical pixel/encoder claim is invented.\n\nFive existing shared-player package records had stale target bytes/SHA. Correct only those registrations and the package aggregate, preserving every source/source_sha256 provenance value and every current payload. The combined package preserves the separately reviewed Rowdy additions; two old-base packages were never sequentially copied over one another. Historical cause of the stale registrations is unknown. The complete catalog/package undo and all285 formal guards protect all native/review pairs and the accepted baseline. No frontend code, dialogue, native field, motion or cross-scene link changes.\n\nThe original preparation tool stdout57a788 accidentally labeled the last guard-loop hash as the merged-package hash. The actual plan and package were correct; merged-package-exact-byte-proof.json retains the correction and exact pathname. The original business installer ran once, exit0; all source and review evidence remains immutable.\n"
